            <div xml:id="d51">

                <pb facs="0145" n="69" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg69"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.47H31/56</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Wellington</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bucklin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 29</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Wellington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-11-16">November 16, 1934</date>.<lb/>[Received December
                        5.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>There has just been handed to me this morning a communication from the Right
                    Honorable J. G. Coates, Minister of Finance and Customs, copy of which
                    communication is transmitted herewith. It will be noted from this communication
                    that the New Zealand Government is desirous of opening conversations with a view
                    to entering into a reciprocal trade agreement. It is found on comparing this
                    communication with the records of the overtures made last year by the New
                    Zealand Government, that this new move is practically a repetition of what was
                    then undertaken, and hence requires no lengthy explanation to the Department,
                    which is doubtless already fully aware of all the features of the case.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Geo</hi>. A. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Bucklin</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d51-a1.xml" xpointer="d51-a1"/>
            </div>
